   "evidence": "GradedAlgebra.lean:87 `private theorem mk_mul_mk_comm`, with the class-level statement at :90\u2013:102. `grep -n 'cup_gradedComm\\|cup_comm'` over TauCeti: the only public commutativity is `Cup/GradedComm.lean:447 theorem cup_gradedComm`, signed. `FieldTheory/GaloisCohomology/MuTwo/Cup.lean:90 kummerCup_comm` re-does the same sign elimination by hand in bidegree (1,1).",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Homological/ContCohomology/Cup/TrivialF2/GradedAlgebra.lean",
   "fix": "Lift `hcup` out as a public theorem (e.g. `TauCeti.trivialF2TopPairing_cup_comm (m n : \u2115) (x y)`) in this file, and have `mk_mul_mk_comm` apply it.",
   "issue": "`hcup` inside the `private` `mk_mul_mk_comm` is the commutativity of the mod-two cup product on classes, `cup m n x y = (degreeCast (Nat.add_comm n m)).hom (cup n m y x)` \u2014 a reusable statement about the public `trivialF2TopPairing`, independent of the graded packaging. Consumers working with `cup` (the whole mod-two corpus: MuTwo, Kummer, corestriction) cannot reach it: the only public commutativity is `cup_gradedComm`, which still carries `((-1)^(m*n)) \u2022`, and recovering the sign-free form through `instGCommRing` requires `of`-injectivity across the degrees `m + n` vs `n + m`.",
   "line": 90
  },
  {
