   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/Homological/ContCohomology/Cup/TrivialF2/GradedAlgebra.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem of_cohomF2One : DirectSum.of (cohomF2 G) 0 (cohomF2One G) = 1`, and reorient the unit lemma as `@[simp] cohomF2One G = (1 : cohomF2 G 0)` (keeping the current statement unannotated if it is still wanted).",
   "issue": "Nothing identifies the unit of `gradedCohomF2 G`: there is no `DirectSum.of (cohomF2 G) 0 (cohomF2One G) = 1`. Worse, `@[simp] gOne_eq_cohomF2One` points away from the algebraic normal form \u2014 it rewrites `(1 : cohomF2 G 0)` (i.e. `GradedMonoid.GOne.one`) into `cohomF2One G`, which pre-empts Mathlib's `@[simp] DirectSum.of_zero_one` and `one_mul` on the grade-zero ring, so `simp` can neither produce nor consume `1` in degree zero.",
